# Linear Workspace: Decision Making Tool

The Linear MCP is connected. Always use it to look up issues before working on tasks.

## Key IDs
- **Workspace:** UCSB Spatial Center
- **Team:** `UCSB Spatial Center` (key: `UCS`)
- **Project:** `Decision Making Tool` (id: `9f249268-5ae4-48e1-871d-7bca6ee1f511`)

## Labels
| Label | Branch / Meaning |
|---|---|
| `foundation` | Core scaffolding, services, layout — branch: `foundation` |
| `solution-controls` | Left sidebar, solution finder — branch: `feat/solution-controls` |
| `map-spatial` | ArcGIS map panel — branch: `feat/map-spatial` |
| `analysis-dashboards` | Right sidebar, metrics, comparison — branch: `feat/analysis-dashboards` |
| `frontend` | All frontend issues (applied alongside branch label) |
| `backend` | Backend/API concerns |
| `CP1`–`CP4` | Checkpoint milestone (CP1=High priority, CP2–4=Medium, stretch=Low) |
| `stretch` | Nice-to-have; defer if time-constrained |

## Issue Naming Convention
Issues follow the format `[PREFIX]-[NN]: [Title]`
- `FND-XX` → foundation branch
- `SOL-XX` → solution-controls branch
- `MAP-XX` → map-spatial branch
- `ANL-XX` → analysis-dashboards branch

## Shorthand Prompts
When the user types these, interpret them as:

| User says | What to do |
|---|---|
| `show [branch]` | `list_issues` filtered by that branch label |
| `show CP1` | `list_issues` filtered by label `CP1` |
| `show [branch] CP1` | `list_issues` filtered by both labels |
| `look up UCS-XX` | `get_issue` by that identifier |
| `done UCS-XX` | `set_task_status` → `done` |
| `new [branch] issue: [title]` | `save_issue` with correct branch + `frontend` labels + team + project |
| `sub UCS-XX: [title]` | `save_issue` with `parentId` of UCS-XX |
| `update UCS-XX: [note]` | `save_issue` appending note to that issue's description |
| `project update: [note]` | `save_project` updating the description's "Current Status" section |

## When Working on a Task
1. Always call `get_issue` with the UCS identifier first
2. Note the labels to understand which branch and checkpoint it belongs to
3. Check `parentId` — if set, this is a sub-task; look up the parent too
